@startuml __#13-02 IPC callback transmission (proxy to remotediag) - code mapped__

title __#13-02 IPC callback transmission (proxy to remotediag)__
!pragma teoz true

autonumber

box "EP" #lightYellow
    participant "<b>XXXMgr Service\n<b>(e.g. DcemqttproxyManagerService)" as XXX #Application
    box "RemotediagProxy" #ffe9b3
        participant "<b>XXXManagerAdapter\n<b>(e.g. MqttManagerAdapter)" as ADP #Application
        participant "<b>ProxyIpcClient" as CLI #Application
        participant "<b>UnixSocketClient\n<b>(rdgipc)" as USC #Application
    endbox
endbox

box "IP" #lightBlue
    box "RemoteDiag" #cfe6ff
        participant "<b>UnixSocketServer\n<b>(rdgipc)" as USS #Application
        participant "<b>ProxyIpcServer" as SRV #Application
        participant "<b>MessageDispatcher\n<b>(mDispatcher)" as DISP #Application
        participant "<b>XXXManagerAdapter\n<b>::CallbackHandler" as CB_HDL #Application
        participant "<b>RemotediagHandler" as RDH #Application
    endbox
endbox

== Callback trigger from XXXMgr (binder callback) ==
XXX->ADP: onNotifyReceived(DceNotification)\n(via registered receiver, e.g. MqttNotifyReceiver)
ADP->ADP: serialize to Parcel\n-> payload (std::vector<uint8_t>)

== Callback publish from proxy (EP) ==
ADP->CLI: ProxyIpcClient::sendCallback(\ncallbackId, payload)
CLI->CLI: lock mCallbackMutex\npush_back mPendingCallbacks\n(max 64, full -> return false)
CLI->CLI: flushCallbacks()\n(best-effort, lock mFlushMutex)
note right of CLI #White
Retry paths if not connected / send failed:
- runCallbackDrainLoop() (mCallbackDrainThread, 100ms)
- onFrameReceived() also calls flushCallbacks()
end note
CLI->USC: sendFrame(Frame{type=Callback,\nmessageId=callbackId, corr=0, payload})
CLI->CLI: mPendingCallbacks.pop_front()\n(after send OK)

== Transport delivery (unix socket) ==
USC->USS: /dev/socket/remotediag/remotediag_proxy.sock\nFrame{type=Callback, id=callbackId, corr=0, payload}
USS->SRV: runReaderLoop()\n-> frameReceivedCallback\n-> onFrameReceived(frame)

== Callback dispatch on remotediag side (IP) ==
SRV->SRV: handleCallback(frame)\npush_back mCallbackQueue (max 64)\nmCallbackQueueCv.notify_one()
SRV->SRV: runCallbackDispatchLoop()\n(mCallbackDispatchThread pops frame)
SRV->DISP: dispatchCallback(\nframe.messageId, frame.payload)
DISP->DISP: lookup mCallbackHandlers[callbackId]\n(registered via registerCallbackHandler()\nin CallbackHandler::initialize())
DISP->CB_HDL: handle(callbackId, payload)
CB_HDL->CB_HDL: deserialize payload\n(Parcel -> DceNotification)
CB_HDL->RDH: obtainMessage(\nMSG_CENTER_PUSH_RECEIVED, dataEvent)\n->sendToTarget()

note over CLI,SRV #White
Callback is one-way (no response frame required):
Frame.messageType = MessageType::Callback, correlationId = 0.
end note

@enduml
